WEBVTT

00:00:08.000 --> 00:00:14.220
Hi, friends. Gani here. This is The Big Change Map.

00:00:14.220 --> 00:00:20.440
Sit tall in your chair. Feet flat on the floor.

00:00:20.440 --> 00:00:24.172
Hands resting on your desk. Shoulders soft.

00:00:24.172 --> 00:00:27.904
Take one slow breath with me… and let it go.

00:00:27.904 --> 00:00:36.612
Sometimes something big changes. A move to a new home. A new school. A new teacher. A new baby in the family. A friend who moves away.

00:00:36.612 --> 00:00:46.563
A big change is not a bad change, and it is not a good change either. It is just big. Big is a size, not a verdict.

00:00:46.563 --> 00:00:57.759
When something feels that big, it helps to have a map. A map shows you where you are — and that you are somewhere, not lost.

00:00:57.759 --> 00:01:02.735
Let me show you the map. It has three territories.

00:01:02.735 --> 00:01:13.931
Territory one: what changed. Name it plainly, inside. The house. The classroom. The faces at the door. Plain and true.

00:01:13.931 --> 00:01:25.127
Territory two: what stayed the same. Your people. Your favorite song. The way your name sounds. And this one matters most: you are still you.

00:01:25.127 --> 00:01:36.323
What stayed the same is the anchor of the map. The change can be big, and the anchor still holds. You carried yourself across.

00:01:36.323 --> 00:01:46.275
Territory three: what we don't know yet. What the new place will feel like. Who you will meet. Some of this, nobody knows — not even grown-ups.

00:01:46.275 --> 00:01:47.519
Not-knowing is a place on the map, not a failure. Every map has an edge where the drawing isn't finished yet.

00:01:47.519 --> 00:01:58.714
You are allowed to miss what changed. Missing is not a problem to fix, and nobody here will argue you out of it.

00:01:58.714 --> 00:02:09.910
You are also allowed to feel two things at once — sad about the old and curious about the new. Both can ride on the same map.

00:02:09.910 --> 00:02:18.618
Nobody has to find the bright side. There is no silver lining you owe anyone. The map does not ask you to be glad.

00:02:18.618 --> 00:02:19.862
Your map is yours. Nobody here will ask you to share it, name it, or explain it. You can walk it quietly, inside.

00:02:19.862 --> 00:02:28.570
What changed. What stayed. What we don't know yet.

00:02:28.570 --> 00:02:34.790
Shoulders soft. Let your body rest.

00:02:34.790 --> 00:02:39.766
Hands down. One more slow breath… and let it go.

00:02:39.766 --> 00:02:45.986
Eyes open. Look around your classroom.

00:02:45.986 --> 00:02:52.206
You're ready for what's next.
